    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξονομ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>utter aloud, announce,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενεήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					59
				</span></i>
			; freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος τ᾽ ἔφατ᾽ ἔκ
				τ᾽ ὀνόμαζε</span> he spoke the word and <i>uttered</i> it
				<i>aloud,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.361
			</span></i>, al.; cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1066
			</span></i>(lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>call by name,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				40
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be referred to by name,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PTeb.
				28.17
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, etc.</div>
